dani (docs): heads-up: PR #4821 has a structured-output example using unions (e.g., string | string[]). a couple of customers reported flaky parsers when responses flip between single value and array. can we pick a recommended pattern? :thinking:

sam (eng): yep saw that. common case is an LLM returning 'foo' sometimes and ['foo'] other times. recommendation: choose one canonical shape in docs and provide a tiny shim for compatibility.

misha (ml): agree. canonicalize to arrays in the schema and examples. arrays are easier to reason about for batching and evals. add a tiny normalize helper for callers that still need to accept older outputs.

kai (devex): i can add an SDK helper (ensureArray) and a one-line example in the JS snippets. that should stop multiple teams from copy-pasting ad-hoc shims.

dani (docs): draft pattern i wrote for the doc (will paste into PR comment):

```
// preferred schema shape (array canonical)
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "items": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
  },
  "required": ["items"]
}

// tiny parser shim for backwards compatibility
function normalizeItems(field) {
  if (field === null || field === undefined) return [];
  return Array.isArray(field) ? field : [field];
}
```

sam (eng): couple notes: 1) mention nullable vs missing — treat null like missing (return []). 2) add a short guardrail: instruct authors in prompts to "Please always output lists as JSON arrays."

misha (ml): also suggest three quick eval prompts: single-item response, multi-item response, explicit null. include those as testcases so model onboarding catches regressions.

kai (devex): PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/devex-sdk/pull/123 — adds ensureArray(field) helper plus unit tests. build-bot: CI started.

build-bot: CI checks queued for kai/devex-sdk#123 (3 checks)

kai (devex): CI passed locally; will push tests. propose SDK snippet for docs: 

```
// using client helper after parse
const parsed = client.parseStructured(resp);
const items = client.ensureArray(parsed.items); // returns [] | [...items]
```

and unit tests: 
```
expect(ensureArray('a')).toEqual(['a']);
expect(ensureArray(['a','b'])).toEqual(['a','b']);
expect(ensureArray(null)).toEqual([]);
```

dani (docs): perfect. i'll update PR #4821 with the array-canonicalization + acceptance-shim wording, add the SDK link (3-line note), and a one-paragraph FAQ entry explaining tradeoffs (arrays preferred; shims for compatibility).

sam (eng): small migration note: add a line to the function-calling migration guide advising teams to remove fragile custom parsers once they upgrade to the SDK helper.

misha (ml): add the sample prompts to the eval checklist as well so model changes don't silently break parsers.

kai (devex): merged devex-sdk#123 — commit: https://github.com/redwood-inference/devex-sdk/commit/7a9fabc (ensureArray implemented). CI green.

dani (docs): thanks! i'll push doc changes today EOD. reviewers: please verify code fences and inline JSON render correctly in the site preview. i'll also include the three eval prompts in the PR description.

sam (eng): can you ping me on the review for wording? quick pass will help avoid ambiguous phrasing.

dani (docs): will do. marking this thread as FYI until docs are live. follow-up once deployed. :white_check_mark:
